A||||9||SCCA FIERO||Twas a good day||||14||
Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||04-17-2000||09:16 PM||||Yesterday at the autocross I mean. People are talking about how the MR2s are great handeling cars and such. Well yesterday my little ole Coupe whipped 3 Mr. 2s. There was another one there that did beat me, but it was heavily modified and was turbo. <P>There were 4 cars, including mine, in C Stock. 2 Miatas and a 96 (I think 96) MR2. The 2 Miatas beat me with my street tires compared to them running slicks. That's my mission... beat the Miata's and put the Coupe in 1st. Another MR2 was in ESP (E Street Prepared...exhaust and intake mods) and my times were faster than his. Another MR2 (89 I think) was running in street tire class, but is still in C Stock which is my class. The closest MR2 was over 2 seconds behind me even with mods and slicks. Worth mentioning is the Inegra Type R that couldn't match my times. It was an actual Type R (2000 model and was yellow)... not like the Type R Neon and Civic that was also there... kinda funny to laugh at them behind their backs  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I have poly bushings that I plan to install one of these days and a 1 inch rear swaybar in the mail. Next I plan to get steel brake lines and lower the car. That should help me catch those darn Miata's.<P>OK, I'm done bragging  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MVC-006S.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000001||GT Bastard||04-17-2000||09:44 PM||||That's what it's all about!<P>AMEN||||reg||14
Z||000002||SloPonti||04-17-2000||10:23 PM||||do you have the four cylinder or six? good job on your wins!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||04-17-2000||11:32 PM||||Good Race! You will be amazed at how better the car will handle with poly bushings. As soon as I install my rear sway I'll let you know about it's effect too!||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChadMan||04-18-2000||09:20 AM||||Nice work!  Maybe you're just a good driver, SCCA - Grassroots Motorsports just printed the results of the Tire Rack Solo II Championships and there wasn't a Fiero in the whole list.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I should be participating in my first autoX with Eric 4/30 if all works out.  My car needs some minor brake work and front tires but I'm going to run it "as is" and establish a baseline.  My goal is to avoid finishing dead last.||||reg||1
Z||000005||bHooper||04-18-2000||09:44 AM||||Good Job, Chris!  Go get em!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Eric||04-18-2000||09:54 AM||||A good starting point, that doesn't cost any money, is extra tire pressure.  If you haven't tried this already, SCCA, put about 40psi in each tire for the first lap dropping air pressure gradually until you get the desired traction.  Some guys use white shoe polish on the sidewall just to see how much the tire is rolling over.  Last year I borrowed an optical perometer to measure the tire temp across the width of the tire.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Patrick||04-18-2000||02:31 PM||||<BR>That looks like fun! <P>All I'd have to do to my Fiero before I could try it would be to upgrade my tires, suspension, brakes, clutch, and engine. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000008||SCCA FIERO||04-18-2000||03:09 PM||||Ptrick, I would still try it once... it's so much fun. You don't HAVE to upgrade anything to your car, I mean, you're not there to earn money. I highly recommend it... not many things I have ever done is as fun.<P>Eric, if you look in my pic you can see the white shoe polish. I run 39 psi in the rear and 37 in the front. With that I get about a 1/4" of roll onto the side wall on each tire. My first lap I ran 42 in the rear and 40 in the front... that was my slowest lap.<P>Chadman, the best advise I can give you is to remember that slow is fast. What I mean is if you are jerking the wheel, hitting the brake and gas hard you will upset the car and have to take a slower line. Exit speed is the key... you can slow down three times as fast as it takes to speed back up. So as you are exiting is where you should try to be fast... not coming into the turn so that you end up missing the apex. Good luck and have fun (I know you will).<P>Sloponti, my car came with a 2.5 but I stuffed a 2.8 from my old 86SE in there.<P>||||reg||7
Z||000009||Patrick||04-18-2000||04:01 PM||||<BR>Chris, you say I don't HAVE to upgrade anything. Trust me, with my Fiero I would! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||14
